  [PASS] V4 [statement]   THE LAW AT HIGH z (G080): on the MSA-3D sample (30 galaxies, z = 0.58-1.68) the zero-parameter equipartition prediction v_flat = (G M_b a0)^(1/4) with the flat DE-anchored a0 = 9.3619e-11 holds WITHOUT a measurable evolutionary drift: log10(v_obs/v_pred) has median +0.21 dex (1-sigma band +0.18..+0.23, N = 30) and a slope -0.032 +- 0.077 dex/z (t = -0.41) -- no significant trend.  The zero point is +0.207 at low z and +0.204 at high z: FLAT in z, i.e. a z-INDEPENDENT zero-point anchor, NOT the rising-a0 signature (which would grow toward +0.33 at z = 2.5 and is already +0.22 at z = 1.5).  The offset sits above BOTH predictions at the point estimate (gas-free stellar mass, IMF/SED systematics +-0.2 dex class), so the absolute anchor is mass-calibration-limited while the trend -- the systematics-cancelling, discriminating statement -- is flat.  A z ~ 2.5 decision needs 1 system(s) at the registered 0.13-dex floor (20:1; pre-registered), about 1 with this sample's observed scatter, 4 for 5-sigma.

